<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  COLLECTION track row - the FINAL 3.6.6 design (F3).

  Frozen `Track Item N`, light node 2409:31563 / dark 2444:18177, reproduced in
  full for the first time: 358x98, r24, on `surface` with a 1px INSIDE stroke on
  `outline`, and three columns.

      0    17          81   97              285  301        341  358
      |    | 64x64 r20 |    | title         |    | 40x40 O  |    |
      |    |  cover    | 16 | artist        | 16 |  ring    | 17 |

  What CHANGED from the Phase B row, and why - the long version is in
  docs/COLLECTION-3.6.6.md:

  **The 64x64 cover is here, and with it the frozen 98dp row.** Phase B recorded
  that this needed "a Room migration plus a per-row fetch". Only the second half
  was ever true: ArtworkRepository keys on artist and track, which FavoriteTrack
  already stores, so nothing about the schema changes. The fetch follows
  PlayerHistoryAdapter exactly - the same repository, the same cancel-on-recycle,
  the same bare plate while it resolves and if it finds nothing.

  **The four inline service buttons and the delete cross are gone from the row.**
  They are not deleted: they are the first five rows of the per-track sheet the
  circular action opens - see CollectionTrackSheet and sheet_collection_track.xml.
  Every destination is the same MusicSearchHelper call it was, and removal is the
  same FavoritesViewModel.removeFavorite it was. The frozen row has exactly one
  control and this is what is behind it.

  **The stream badge is gone.** It was retained through Phase B as an accepted
  deviation, to be settled by this migration; the frozen row has no counterpart
  for it and neither does the frozen sheet, whose two text lines are the track
  and the artist. The station it carried is still written by the CSV export,
  which is where the value was always duplicated. Owner decision.

  **The separator is gone** with the control strip it separated.

  **Truncation is unchanged**, deliberately: one line for the title, two for the
  artist. The frozen row specifies neither ellipsis nor maxLines, only fixed 18
  and 16 boxes against 28 and 20 line heights - the authoring pathology B2
  refused to reproduce on the Mini Player title. The boxes are applied as minima
  so the tokens' real line boxes are honoured and no glyph is clipped. Whether
  Collection adopts History's variable-height, never-truncate rule is still a
  separate decision, and CollectionLayoutTest asserts F3 did not take it either.

  The row height is a MINIMUM, so a wrapped artist grows the row rather than
  clipping; one-line content measures the frozen 17 + 64 + 17 = 98.
-->
<com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:id="@+id/collection_row"
    style="@style/CollectionCard"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:layout_marginBottom="@dimen/collection_row_gap">

    <androidx.constraintlayout.widget.ConstraintLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:minHeight="@dimen/collection_row_min_height"
        android:padding="@dimen/collection_card_padding">

        <!--
          `Container` at (17,17), 64x64 r20, holding an IMAGE fill. Pinned to the
          top rather than centred: the frozen cover's top edge is the row's own
          17 padding, and on a row that has grown for a second artist line the
          cover must stay on that padding rather than drift down with the text.
        -->
        <com.google.android.material.imageview.ShapeableImageView
            android:id="@+id/artwork"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/collection_row_artwork_size"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/collection_row_artwork_size"
            android:background="@drawable/bg_collection_row_artwork"
            android:contentDescription="@string/collection_row_artwork"
            android:scaleType="centerCrop"
            app:layout_constraintStart_toStartOf="parent"
            app:layout_constraintTop_toTopOf="parent"
            app:shapeAppearanceOverlay="@style/ShapeAppearance.Myata.CollectionRowArtwork" />

        <!--
          `Container` at (97,32), 188x34, holding `Heading 3` over the artist.
          Centred as a block against the cover, which is what the frozen 32 is:
          the 34 text block on a 98 row inside 17 padding sits 15 below the
          cover's top and 15 above its bottom.

          The 188 width is not pinned. It is what is left between the cover and
          the action, which resolves to exactly 188 at 390dp and to the right
          answer at 320, 360 and 412 - a fixed 188 would be wrong at all four.
        -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/text_column"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/collection_row_gutter"
            android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/collection_row_gutter"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            app:layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf="parent"
            app:layout_constraintEnd_toStartOf="@id/btn_row_action"
            app:layout_constraintStart_toEndOf="@id/artwork"
            app:layout_constraintTop_toTopOf="parent">

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tv_track"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:minHeight="@dimen/collection_row_title_min_height"
                android:text="Track Title"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Regular.16_28"
                android:textColor="@color/text_primary" />

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tv_artist"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:maxLines="2"
                android:minHeight="@dimen/collection_row_artist_min_height"
                android:text="ARTIST NAME"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Regular.12_20"
                android:textColor="@color/text_secondary" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <!--
          `Container > Button` at (301,29), 40x40, r=9999, no fill, 2px INSIDE
          stroke on `primary`, holding `arrow_forward` rotated 45 degrees.

          Centred against the cover rather than against the row: the frozen 29 on
          a 98 row puts its centre at 49, which is the cover's centre (17 + 32),
          and that is the alignment that survives the row growing.

          40 is below the 48dp touch minimum. The ring keeps its drawn 40 and
          FavoritesAdapter expands the target to 48 with a TouchDelegate - the
          same answer docs/COLLECTION-3.6.6.md reached for the header overflow,
          where a 4x16 glyph lives inside a 48dp slot.
        -->
        <ImageView
            android:id="@+id/btn_row_action"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/collection_row_action_size"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/collection_row_action_size"
            android:background="@drawable/bg_collection_row_action"
            android:contentDescription="@string/collection_row_action"
            android:scaleType="center"
            android:src="@drawable/ic_collection_row_action"
            app:layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf="@id/artwork"
            app:layout_constraintEnd_toEndOf="parent"
            app:layout_constraintTop_toTopOf="@id/artwork"
            app:tint="@color/primary" />

    </androidx.constraintlayout.widget.ConstraintLayout>

</com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>
